<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turicum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Turicum was the Roman settlement on the site of modern Zürich, at the outflow of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limmat">Limmat</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-zurich">Lake Zurich</a>. It held a customs station collecting the duty on goods passing between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raetia">Raetia</a>. In the late Roman period a fort stood on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindenhof">Lindenhof</a> hill, which remained the centre of the early medieval town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turicum.jpg" alt="Turicum" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland zh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Weinplatz_-_Lindenhof_-_Schipfe_-_Limmatquai_2015-02-26_12-41-21.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
